@startuml requirement-issue-states
' cumin-works - the states of a requirement issue, with the action names only.
' Each category page holds the guards and what cumin does (plan, acceptance).
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/".
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
state "ready" as Ready
state "planning" as Planning
state "awaiting-plan-review" as PlanReview
state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : the sub-issues are in work
state "accepting" as Accepting
state "awaiting-acceptance" as AwaitingAcceptance
state "awaiting-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready
Ready --> Planning : request the split
Planning --> Planning : request the split again
Planning --> PlanReview : ask for the plan review
Planning --> Decision : stop the split
Draft --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work
PlanReview --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work
Implementing --> PlanReview : ask about the remaining sub-issues
Planning --> Accepting : request the acceptance check
Implementing --> Accepting : request the acceptance check
PlanReview --> Accepting : request the acceptance check
Accepting --> Accepting : request the acceptance check again
Accepting --> AwaitingAcceptance : ask for the acceptance
Accepting --> PlanReview : ask for the plan review
Accepting --> Decision : stop the acceptance check
AwaitingAcceptance --> Implementing : send back
AwaitingAcceptance --> [*] : the Assignee closes the issue
Decision --> Ready : the Assignee answers and adds ready

@enduml
